<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`PEnt`).** Entailment in the powerset holds when the output integer already belongs to the input finite set.


**Definition (`bar`).** The bar.


**Definition (`P`).** The powerset domain has the natural numbers as tokens, every finite set consistent, and the least entailment.


**Theorem (`P.AllConsistent`).** The statement all Consistent holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Definition (`IdemApprox`).** The idem Approx.


**Definition (`ReflApprox`).** The refl Approx.


**Definition (`barElement`).** The bar Element.


**Definition (`powersetBot`).** The bot Element.


**Definition (`powersetTop`).** The top Element.


**Definition (`ConsistentApprox`).** The consistent Approx.


**Definition (`BotApprox`).** A bottom approximation is the approximable map that entails only what the empty set entails.


**Definition (`RogueApprox`).** A rogue approximation relates some token to the reserved top token.


**Definition (`IsDomainApprox`).** The is Domain Approx are given by the listed constructors.


**Definition (`DomainApprox`).** A domain approximation is an approximable self-map of the powerset that is reflexive, transitive, and not rogue.


**Definition (`flatRel`).** The flat relation on the powerset is the least entailment.


**Theorem (`flatRel.empty`).** The empty of the empty set is empty.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`flatRel.of_mem_one`).** The statement of mem one holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`mem_barElement`).** A token lies in the mem bar Element exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`mem_topElement`).** A token lies in the mem top Element exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Definition (`scottCon`).** The scott Con.


**Theorem (`BotApprox_any`).** The statement bot Approx any holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Definition (`flatMap`).** The flat map is the approximable map of the least entailment.


**Theorem (`flatMap.consistent`).** The statement consistent holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`flatMap.idem`).** The statement idem holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`flatMap.refl`).** The statement refl holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`flatMap.toElement_of_mem_one`).** The statement to Element of mem one holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`flatMap.rogue`).** The statement rogue holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`flatMap.isDomain`).** The statement is Domain holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Definition (`flatDomainApprox`).** The flat Domain Approx.


**Theorem (`mem_botElement`).** A token lies in the mem bot Element exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`not_RogueApprox_idMap`).** The claim not Rogue Approx id Map fails.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`barElement_zero_eq_bot`).** The equality bar Element zero eq bot holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`scottCon_empty_iff_consistent`).** The scott Con empty iff consistent of the empty set is empty.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □
